        "/Users/brad/.cache/swarm-comparison/tools/swarm/dist/cli.js",
        "With the configuration unknown-options-as-args: true, arguments that are not recognised options are placed into the positional array _ instead of being parsed as flags. When boolean-negation is additionally set to false, the --no-<name> negation syntax is disabled, so --no-known-arg can no longer refer to the declared boolean known-arg and must be treated as an unknown option. Today it is still recognised and produces knownArg: false. Required: parser(\"--no-known-arg --no-unknown-arg\", { boolean: [\"known-arg\"], configuration: { \"unknown-options-as-args\": true, \"boolean-negation\": false } }) must return exactly { _: [\"--no-known-arg\", \"--no-unknown-arg\"] }. With boolean-negation left at its default, behavior must not change (--no-known-arg still yields knownArg: false). Source is lib/yargs-parser.ts; tests are compiled with npx tsc -p tsconfig.test.json and run with npm test (mocha).\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): npx tsc -p tsconfig.test.json && node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npm test\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/.",
